          "question": "With reference to international climate negotiations under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) and the Paris Agreement, consider the following statements:\n1. The 'New Collective Quantified Goal' (NCQG) on climate finance agreed at UNFCCC COP29 in Baku calls on developed countries to take the lead in mobilizing at least USD 300 billion per year by 2035 for developing countries, within a broader scaling target of USD 1.3 trillion per year.\n2. Article 6.4 of the Paris Agreement establishes a centralized, UN-supervised global carbon credit mechanism (Paris Agreement Crediting Mechanism) replacing the Kyoto Protocol's Clean Development Mechanism (CDM).\n3. In India, the domestic Carbon Credit Trading Scheme (CCTS) was notified by the Central Government under the Environment (Protection) Act, 1986 with the Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB) as its sole administrator.\n\nWhich of the statements given above are correct?",
