          "question": "With reference to the High-Level Committee on Simultaneous Elections ('One Nation, One Election') chaired by former President Ram Nath Kovind, consider the following statements:\n1. The Committee recommended a two-step implementation: in the first step, elections to the House of the People (Lok Sabha) and all State Legislative Assemblies are synchronized; in the second step, elections to Municipalities and Panchayats are held within 100 days of the general election.\n2. It proposed inserting Article 82A into the Constitution, whereby if a House is dissolved sooner than its full five-year term, the fresh election held to constitute the new House shall be only for the 'unexpired term' of the immediately preceding full term.\n3. According to the Committee, neither the synchronization of Lok Sabha and State Assembly elections nor the synchronization of local body elections requires any ratification by the State Legislatures under Article 368(2).\n\nWhich of the statements given above are correct?",
