          "question": "With reference to the Goods and Services Tax (GST) Council constituted under Article 279A of the Constitution (inserted by the 101st Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016), consider the following statements:\n1. Every decision of the GST Council is taken at a meeting by a majority of not less than three-fourths (75%) of the weighted votes of the members present and voting, where the Central Government holds a weightage of one-third (33.33%) and all State Governments together hold a weightage of two-thirds (66.67%).\n2. In 'Union of India vs. Mohit Minerals', the Supreme Court held that recommendations of the GST Council under Article 279A have only persuasive value and are not binding mandates that override the concurrent legislative power of Parliament and State Legislatures under Article 246A.\n3. Petroleum crude, high-speed diesel, motor spirit (petrol), natural gas, and aviation turbine fuel are completely excluded from the purview of Article 279A and can only be brought under GST by a new Constitutional Amendment under Article 368.\n\nWhich of the statements given above are correct?",
