          "explanation": "Statements 2 and 3 are correct; Statement 1 is incorrect.\n• Statement 1 is incorrect: Article 200 explicitly states that a Governor can return a Bill for reconsideration ONLY if it is 'not a Money Bill'.\n• Statements 2 and 3 are correct: In 'State of Punjab vs. Principal Secretary to the Governor of Punjab', the Supreme Court held that if a Governor decides to withhold assent under the substantive part of Article 200, the mandatory course under the first proviso ('as soon as possible') must be followed to return the Bill to the Legislature; if re-passed, the Governor cannot withhold assent or subsequently reserve it for the President.",
          "source": "Article 200 of the Constitution & Supreme Court Judgments",
