          "question": "With reference to ISRO's Aditya-L1 solar mission and the physics of Lagrange points, consider the following statements:\n1. Aditya-L1 is placed in a periodic Halo Orbit around the Sun–Earth Lagrange Point 1 (L1), located approximately 1.5 million kilometres from the Earth towards the Sun, enabling continuous observation of the Sun without any occultation or eclipses.\n2. The Visible Emission Line Coronagraph (VELC), developed by the Indian Institute of Astrophysics (IIA), is the primary payload onboard Aditya-L1 designed to study the diagnostic parameters of the solar corona and the origin of Coronal Mass Ejections (CMEs).\n3. Out of the seven scientific payloads onboard Aditya-L1, four payloads directly view the Sun as remote-sensing instruments, while three payloads perform in-situ measurements of particles and magnetic fields at L1.\n\nWhich of the statements given above are correct?",
