          "subject": "Mental Ability & Reasoning",
          "topic": "Speed, Distance & Time (Vande Bharat Express)",
          "question_type": "Analytical & Quantitative",
          "question": "A Vande Bharat Express train 240 meters long crosses a telegraph pole in 8 seconds. How long will it take to cross a railway bridge 660 meters long at the same uniform speed?",
          "options": [
            "22 seconds",
            "25 seconds",
            "30 seconds",
            "35 seconds"
          ],
          "correct_index": 2,
          "explanation": "Step-by-step calculation:\n• Speed of the train = Length of train / Time to cross pole = 240 m / 8 s = 30 m/s.\n• Total distance to cross the bridge = Length of train + Length of bridge = 240 m + 660 m = 900 m.\n• Time required = 900 m / 30 m/s = 30 seconds.",
