          "question": "With reference to India's Balance of Payments (BoP) accounting and Foreign Exchange Reserves managed by the Reserve Bank of India, consider the following statements:\n1. Private remittances sent home by Non-Resident Indians (NRIs) working abroad and net software service exports are recorded under the 'Invisibles' component of the Current Account, not the Capital Account.\n2. India's official Foreign Exchange Reserves comprise four components: Foreign Currency Assets (FCA), Gold reserves, Special Drawing Rights (SDRs), and Reserve Tranche Position (RTP) with the International Monetary Fund (IMF).\n3. A depreciation of the Indian Rupee against the US Dollar in the spot market automatically increases the dollar valuation of RBI's existing Euro and Pound Sterling assets.\n\nWhich of the statements given above are correct?",
