          "topic": "Telecommunications Act, 2023 & Spectrum Allocation",
          "question_type": "Multi-Statement Analysis",
          "question": "With reference to the Telecommunications Act, 2023 (which replaces the Indian Telegraph Act, 1885 and the Indian Wireless Telegraphy Act, 1933), consider the following statements:\n1. While auction is the default mechanism for spectrum assignment, the First Schedule of the Act specifically authorizes 'administrative allocation' (without auction) of spectrum for satellite-based communication services including Global Mobile Personal Communication by Satellites (GMPCS).\n2. Under the Act, the 'Universal Service Obligation Fund' (USOF) has been renamed 'Digital Bharat Nidhi', which can be utilized not only for rural telecom access but also for research and development of telecommunication technologies and pilot projects.\n3. The Act strips the Central Government of all powers to intercept messages or temporarily take possession of telecom networks on grounds of public emergency or national security.\n\nWhich of the statements given above are correct?",
