          "explanation": "Only three pairs (Pairs 1, 2, and 3) are correctly matched; Pair 4 is incorrect.\n• Pairs 1, 2, and 3 are correct: Bhattiprolu (Pratipalapura) yielded pre-Ashokan/Ashokan-era southern Brahmi caskets mentioning King Kuberaka; Nagarjunakonda (Vijayapuri) was the Ikshvaku capital; Salihundam on the Vamsadhara river in Srikakulam was a major port-monastery site.\n• Pair 4 is incorrect: Thotlakonda and Bavikonda are coastal hilltop Buddhist monastic complexes overlooking the Bay of Bengal in VISAKHAPATNAM district (not Kurnool district).",
