          "question": "Consider the following statements regarding the three criminal laws—Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS), and Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam (BSA):\n1. Under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS), the visit of a forensic expert to the crime scene to collect forensic evidence is mandatory for all offences punishable with imprisonment of seven years or more.\n2. The Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) introduces 'Community Service' as a statutory form of punishment for minor offences such as petty theft and public intoxication.\n3. Under Article 20(1) of the Constitution, substantive criminal offences newly created under the BNS apply retrospectively to acts committed prior to July 1, 2024.\n\nWhich of the statements given above are correct?",
