          "question": "Consider the following statements regarding tribal welfare missions and Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs) in Andhra Pradesh:\n1. The Pradhan Mantri Janjati Adivasi Nyaya Maha Abhiyan (PM-JANMAN) targets socio-economic saturation of 75 PVTGs across 18 States and the UT of Andaman & Nicobar Islands through 11 critical interventions implemented by 9 Ministries.\n2. Out of the tribal communities residing in Andhra Pradesh, six groups—Chenchu, Gadaba, Khond, Konda Reddi, Konda Savara, and Porja—are officially notified as PVTGs (including their sub-groups).\n3. Scheduled Areas in Andhra Pradesh are administered under the Sixth Schedule of the Constitution through Autonomous District Councils.\n\nHow many of the statements given above are correct?",
