          "correct_index": 1,
          "explanation": "Only two statements (Statements 1 and 2) are correct; Statement 3 is incorrect.\n• Statement 1 is correct: PM-JANMAN (outlay Rs. 24,104 crore) focuses specifically on 75 PVTGs across 18 States and A&N Islands via 11 interventions of 9 Ministries, complemented by the broader Dharti Aaba Janjatiya Gram Utkarsh Abhiyan (Rs. 79,156 crore across ~63,000 villages).\n• Statement 2 is correct: The notified PVTGs of Andhra Pradesh are Chenchu, Bodo Gadaba/Gutob Gadaba, Dongria Khond/Kutia Khond, Konda Reddi, Konda Savara, and Bondo Porja/Khodu Porja/Parengi Porja.\n• Statement 3 is incorrect: Scheduled Areas in Andhra Pradesh are governed under the FIFTH Schedule (Article 244(1)) and the PESA Act, 1996 (not the Sixth Schedule, which applies only to Assam, Meghalaya, Tripura, and Mizoram).",
