          "question": "Consider the following statements regarding irrigation and river-linking projects in Andhra Pradesh:\n1. The Pattiseema Lift Irrigation Scheme lifts floodwater from the Godavari River upstream of the Dowleswaram Barrage and delivers it into the Polavaram Right Main Canal, which drops into the Krishna River at Pavitra Sangamam (Ibrahimpatnam) upstream of the Prakasam Barrage.\n2. The proposed Godavari–Banakacherla Link Project aims to divert surplus Godavari floodwaters via the Krishna (Nagarjunasagar/Bollapalli) to the Banakacherla Cross Regulator in Nandyal district to drought-proof Rayalaseema.\n3. The Handri–Neeva Sujala Sravanthi (HNSS) project lifts water from the Somasila Reservoir on the Penna River to irrigate Srikakulam and Vizianagaram districts.\n\nWhich of the statements given above are correct?",
