          "question": "Engineer Team A can complete a section of the Polavaram feeder canal in 20 days, and Engineer Team B can complete the same section in 30 days. They work together for 8 days, after which Team A leaves. In how many days will Team B alone finish the remaining work?",
          "options": [
            "8 days",
            "10 days",
            "12 days",
            "15 days"
          ],
          "correct_index": 1,
          "explanation": "Step-by-step calculation:\n• A's 1 day work = 1/20; B's 1 day work = 1/30.\n• Combined 1 day work of (A + B) = 1/20 + 1/30 = (3 + 2)/60 = 5/60 = 1/12.\n• Work done in 8 days together = 8 × (1/12) = 2/3.\n• Remaining work = 1 - 2/3 = 1/3.\n• Time taken by B alone to finish 1/3 work = (1/3) / (1/30) = 10 days.",
          "source": "APPSC Prelims CSAT / Mental Ability Official Pattern",
