          "correct_index": 0,
          "explanation": "Statements 1 and 2 are correct; Statement 3 is incorrect.\n• Statement 1 is correct: Article 279A(9) sets the voting weightage: Centre = 1/3rd, States combined = 2/3rds, requiring a >=3/4ths (75%) weighted majority.\n• Statement 2 is correct: In Mohit Minerals (2022), the Supreme Court emphasized 'uncooperative federalism' / collaborative federalism under Article 246A.\n• Statement 3 is incorrect: Under Article 279A(5), the five petroleum products (crude oil, high-speed diesel, petrol, natural gas, and ATF) are ALREADY included in the constitutional scheme—the GST Council itself is empowered to recommend the date from which GST shall be levied on them without requiring any new Constitutional Amendment.",
